<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The factory's own vocabulary, and nothing else. `WorkItem`, `Round`, `Swimlane`,
    `Decision`, `Escalation`, `DerivedResult` — the words in CONTEXT.md, in code, with
    no knowledge of how anything is stored, scheduled, called or rendered.

    **This project has no project reference at all.** Not to Application, not to
    Infrastructure, not to Web, and not to a package: nothing in here can be handed a
    seam, because a type that cannot name a seam cannot depend on one. That absence is
    the whole property the layering exists for, and it is the one edge in the graph
    there is no way to add later without a slice deciding it deliberately
    (docs/architecture.md, "The dependency rule").

    TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, LangVersion, TreatWarningsAsErrors and
    IsPackable are in Directory.Build.props; this file says only what is true of this
    project alone, which today is its name. Package versions are in
    Directory.Packages.props — there are none.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>AgentFactory.Domain</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>